{"question": "Sau khi chẩn đoán trật khớp bên (lateral luxation) răng vĩnh viễn không kèm gãy ổ răng, loại máng nẹp nào và thời gian bao lâu được khuyến cáo để cố định?", "claim": "Đối với răng bị trật khớp bên không có gãy ổ răng kèm theo, cần cố định bằng máng nẹp linh hoạt, thụ động trong thời gian bốn tuần với dây thép không gỉ dày tối đa 0,4 mm.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu chuyên môn chỉ định sử dụng máng nẹp linh hoạt thụ động trong 4 tuần với dây thép không quá 0.4 mm cho răng trật khớp bên không gãy xương ổ."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Figure 1 shows the number of correct answers per question, with color coding applied using the traffic light system. Questions 9 (coronoroot fracture) and 10 (simple crown fractures) had the highest numbers of correct answers (88.4% and 75.4%, respectively). In comparison, question 5 (expulsion without associated alveolar fracture) and question 12 (lateral luxation) had the lowest numbers of correct answers (23.2% and 14.4% respectively)."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Lateral luxations are among the most common periodontal lesions in the event of dental trauma. The correct diagnosis, followed by the repositioning of the tooth in the correct position, is fundamental for the healing of the periodontal ligament. Incorrect repositioning of the tooth can lead to poor alveolar healing and chronic pain due to apical fenestration [20]. According to the IADT and the American Association of Endodontists, teeth with lateral luxation without associated alveolar fractures should be stabilized using a passive, flexible splint for four weeks, typically with a stainless-steel wire no thicker than 0.4 mm [8,21]. For cases involving alveolar fractures, the IADT also recommends a flexible splint for four weeks. In a multivariate study of 71 teeth with alveolar fractures, neither the type of splint nor the duration of fixation significantly affected the development of pu"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q3", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "lp necrosis or pulp canal obliteration [22]. Given that teeth with lateral luxation inherently involve alveolar fractures, the splinting recommendation applies consistently to both types of trauma [22]."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "The Knowledge of Traumatic Dental Injury Management Among Dentists in Casablanca-Settat, Morocco: A Cross-Sectional Study Based on the 2020 International Association of Dental Traumatology (IADT) Guidelines", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "The Knowledge of Traumatic Dental Injury Management Among Dentists in Casablanca-Settat, Morocco: A Cross-Sectional Study Based on the 2020 International Association of Dental Traumatology (IADT) Guidelines", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion"]}]}
