{"question": "Mối liên quan giữa viêm nha chu và suy tim được chi phối bởi yếu tố độc lực nào của vi khuẩn Porphyromonas gingivalis?", "claim": "Mối liên quan giữa viêm nha chu và suy tim được thúc đẩy bởi các yếu tố độc lực của vi khuẩn Porphyromonas gingivalis, đặc biệt là các enzyme gingipains gây tổn hại tính toàn vẹn mạch máu và độc tính tế bào cơ tim.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu lâm sàng ghi nhận vi khuẩn Porphyromonas gingivalis tiết ra gingipains phá vỡ liên kết mạch máu và gây độc trực tiếp cho tế bào cơ tim ở bệnh nhân suy tim."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Figure 6. Porphyromonas gingivalis infection Alters autophagy-lysosomal system accelerating the development of NAFLD."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "The severity of periodontitis is significantly associated with increased all-cause and cardiovascular mortality in patients with HF, with research reporting substantially elevated all-cause mortality rates among patients with periodontitis compared with those without periodontal disease (42). Mechanistically, this relationship is driven by bacterial virulence factors, particularly gingipains, cysteine proteinases including arginine-specific and lysine-specific variants produced by Porphyromonas gingivalis. Following hematogenous dissemination, these proteases disrupt vascular integrity through cleavage of critical adherens junction proteins such as vascular endothelial-cadherin, resulting in increased endothelial permeability, enhanced monocyte infiltration, and accelerated atherosclerotic progression, collectively elevating myocardial workload and ischemic susceptibility in HF-prone ind"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q3", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "ividuals (43). Beyond these vascular effects, gingipains exert direct cardiotoxic actions by impairing autophagic flux in cardiomyocytes via proteolytic degradation of essential autophagosomal proteins, vesicle-associated membrane protein 8 and syntaxin-17, leading to accumulated mitochondrial damage and potentiated apoptotic signaling. Experimental models of myocardial infarction demonstrate that Porphyromonas gingivalis infection significantly exacerbates infarct size and"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Impact of Porphyromonas gingivalis-odontogenic infection on the pathogenesis of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease", "heading_path": ["Body", "Proposed mechanisms of pathogenetic role of P. gingivalis infection on NAFLD", "Altering autophagy-lysosomal system"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Association between periodontitis and heart failure: Mechanisms and clinical implications (Review)", "heading_path": ["Body", "Core mechanistic pathways of the ‘periodontal-cardiac axis’", "Direct cardiotoxicity of bacterial virulence factors"]}]}
